{:edb/db-before-t 1429 :edb/db-after-t 1430 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534742 50 #inst "2026-10-08T05:35:55.661Z" 13194139534742 true] [17592186096382 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1 \\\\ y+z=-2 \\\\ -x+2y+z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534742 true] [17592186096382 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$x - y + z = 1; y + z =-2; - x + 2y + z =-1$.\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534742 false] [17592186096382 1145 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nM\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} + R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{3} \\mid:=R_{3} + (-1)R_{2}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\nx - y + z = 1; y + z =-2; z = 2\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=2$ tells us the value of $z$. Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny + (2) =-2⟹y =-4\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-4$ and $z=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx - (-4) + (2) = 1⟹x =-5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5$, $y=-4$, and $z=2$. Or, in vector form, $\\langle -5,-4,2 \\rangle$." 13194139534742 false] [17592186096382 1145 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1 \\\\ y+z=-2 \\\\ z=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=2$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+(2)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-4$ and $z=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-4)+(2)=1\\,⟹\\,x=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5,$ $y=-4,$ and $z=2.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -5,-4,2 \\rangle.$" 13194139534742 true] [17592186096383 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=-2 \\\\  & x+y+2z=-1 \\\\  & x+2y+z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534742 true] [17592186096383 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n$x + y + z =-2; x + y + 2z =-1; x + 2y + z = 1$.\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534742 false] [17592186096383 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get $a_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=-2 \\\\ y=3 \\\\ z=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z,$ and the second equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting these values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(3)+(1)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-6,$ $y=3,$ and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,3,1 \\rangle.$" 13194139534742 true] [17592186096383 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nM\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{2} + (-1)R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{3} \\mid:=R_{3} + (-1)R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNote that we get $a_{22}=0$. Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n$M\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2}\\end{vmatrix}↔R_{3}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\nx + y + z =-2; y = 3; z = 1\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z$, and the second equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y$. Substituting these values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx + (3) + (1) =-2⟹x =-6\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-6$, $y=3$, and $z=1$. Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,3,1 \\rangle$." 13194139534742 false] [17592186096593 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307006 13194139534742 true] [17592186096593 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307013 13194139534742 true] [17592186096593 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307020 13194139534742 true] [17592186096593 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307027 13194139534742 true] [17592186096594 1020 #edb/ref 17592186306993 13194139534742 true] [17592186096594 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307034 13194139534742 true] [17592186096594 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307041 13194139534742 true] [17592186096594 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307048 13194139534742 true] [17592186097101 1017 #edb/ref 17592186095012 13194139534742 false] [17592186097101 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307000 13194139534742 true] [17592186097101 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534742 true] [17592186097101 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y+6z=5 \\\\  & y-10z=-11 \\\\  & 4x+8y+13z=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." 13194139534742 true] [17592186097101 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n${x + 2y + 6z = 5; y - 10z =-11; 4x + 8y + 13z = 9$\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." 13194139534742 false] [17592186097101 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 13 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 13 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{11}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534742 true] [17592186097269 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534742 true] [17592186097269 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y+2z=8 \\\\  & -2x+2y-3z=-11 \\\\  & x+z=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534742 true] [17592186097269 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n${x - y + 2z = 8; - 2x + 2y - 3z =-11; x + z = 9$.\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534742 false] [17592186097269 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z=8 \\\\ y-z=1 \\\\ z=5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=5$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(5)=1\\,⟹\\,y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=6$ and $z=5$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(6)+2(5)=8\\,⟹\\,x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5.$" 13194139534742 true] [17592186306993 1017 #edb/ref 17592186306994 13194139534742 true] [17592186306993 1089 "q-130927" 13194139534742 true] [17592186306993 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534742 true] [17592186306993 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y-z=4 \\\\  & -3x-6y+4z=-8 \\\\  & 3x+7y-z=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534742 true] [17592186306993 1113 #uuid "8eff9d12-5ab8-5d85-973e-0e821294f176" 13194139534742 true] [17592186306993 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z=4 \\\\ y+2z=-2 \\\\ z=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+2(4)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-10$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2(-10)-(4)=4\\,⟹\\,x=28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4.$" 13194139534742 true] [17592186306994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306995 13194139534742 true] [17592186306994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306996 13194139534742 true] [17592186306994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306997 13194139534742 true] [17592186306994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306998 13194139534742 true] [17592186306994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306999 13194139534742 true] [17592186306994 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534742 true] [17592186306994 1041 "selection" 13194139534742 true] [17592186306994 1104 #edb/ref 17592186306996 13194139534742 true] [17592186306994 1110 #uuid "27ead658-1607-5e21-bef8-9859ed283c4d" 13194139534742 true] [17592186306995 1034 "$x=-12$, $y=6$, and $z=-4$" 13194139534742 true] [17592186306995 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534742 true] [17592186306995 1111 #uuid "237aa6f1-4bcf-54d7-a265-35842fd96b97" 13194139534742 true] [17592186306996 1034 "$x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4$" 13194139534742 true] [17592186306996 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534742 true] [17592186306996 1111 #uuid "a9b32cd9-62b8-5cda-8c27-344ecb042797" 13194139534742 true] [17592186306997 1034 "$x=-12$, $y=-10$, and $z=2$" 13194139534742 true] [17592186306997 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534742 true] [17592186306997 1111 #uuid "7a77cf3d-adf9-549d-960c-c60db24c45dd" 13194139534742 true] [17592186306998 1034 "$x=28$, $y=-6$, and $z=4$" 13194139534742 true] [17592186306998 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534742 true] [17592186306998 1111 #uuid "3f210db8-3b25-5f8e-8b04-4326d3813eaf" 13194139534742 true] [17592186306999 1034 "$x=18$, $y=6$, and $z=2$" 13194139534742 true] [17592186306999 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534742 true] [17592186306999 1111 #uuid "1b2ad833-e3f0-5fe8-9a5e-bce6a9cadabc" 13194139534742 true] [17592186307000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307001 13194139534742 true] [17592186307000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307002 13194139534742 true] [17592186307000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307003 13194139534742 true] [1